[gd_scene load_steps=5 format=3]

; GENERATED â€” the outer forest that hides the edge of the world.
;
; Before this, the treeline stopped at +/-20 and you could see the world simply end behind it.
; These trees sit OUTSIDE the play area (radius 24..52) on the widened 110 m visual ground, so
; they read as depth rather than as a wall. The player never reaches them: the Barriers still
; stop at +/-21.
;
; NO COLLISION on any of it, deliberately â€” the Barriers remain the only thing bounding the play
; space (tests/test_village_boundaries.gd:17). Collision out here would be invisible to the
; player and could only cause bugs.
;
; A deliberate GAP is left on the north side (x -7..7 beyond z=-24) so the way to the shore reads
; as an opening in the forest rather than a wall the player is expected to walk into. ExitToShore
; sits at z=-21, and the story sends the player north.
;
; Deterministic: generated by a fixed-seed LCG (seed 20260814), so regenerating gives the same
; forest. Rings, jitter and species mix are in the generator; to reshape the forest, change those
; and regenerate rather than hand-editing 100+ nodes here.
